{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DYK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-smooth}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:28cbfe2e9f54011f665789daec3b2c705068e0de95afb78ecddc09f25f9bedd3", "source_text": "Smooth or unobstructed categories", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30dd495be552a0965c068a02ca7e09951bdaedd823d10a44877e83d8af6e8fc7", "unit_id": "tag:0DYK:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DYK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9a878a8fc272e472ecf5f4b5ffd8b53691b59c44e9093040af089721ca6a20d2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4988e0a886943d1cff9a1ab00107e5f69036c41c6dbeee7cb25e2183dfd37ad", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in\ngroupoids. We can consider <MATH_0002> as a category\ncofibered in groupoids over <MATH_0003> using the identity\nfunctor. In this way\n<MATH_0004>\nbecomes\na morphism of categories cofibered in groupoids over <MATH_0005>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7570f4b0b5ddbb2ec4118531f549d55396132c1f9901e573d9ee0606226f6a00", "unit_id": "tag:0DYK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0DYK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-smooth-morphism}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cofibered-groupoid-projection-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:24d6265113a7f44dee3b85f15d7eaf523dbab2121b2c522f51b3540dd1aa8a62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bb8241f3089d890b75d863f2d271e9bc10ca64397dbcfb74d785314aaa022f19", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in\ngroupoids. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or <TEXTITOPEN_0002>unobstructed<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif its structure morphism <MATH_0003> is smooth\nin the sense of Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e751a7b1bfe7f94325c4db8591013dfa9f23736eb6173243a44d89a43ca170ee", "unit_id": "tag:06HP:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DYK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cfaf2c68859df93a9943f203016a4cf7eb7189f6d2775102c781b5d2b0ae7b6c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30735946ec856b766d72144c2218dfebbbe7de3763aa5ca82fca5ab16e8ae798", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is the ``absolute'' notion of smoothness for a\ncategory cofibered in groupoids over <MATH_0001>, although\nit would be more correct to say that <MATH_0002> is smooth over <MATH_0003>.\nOne has to be careful with the phrase ``<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0004> is unobstructed<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>'':\nit may happen that\n<MATH_0005> has an obstruction theory with nonvanishing obstruction spaces\neven though <MATH_0006> is smooth.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7076d231318d8e9ccdfea5ccc23cf457a339d2454a4b53ca7c16b03c4bf0f14", "unit_id": "tag:0DYK:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0DYK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0005": "$p: \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal U \\xrightarrow{\\varphi} \\mathcal{F} \\xrightarrow{p}\n\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-essentially-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-properties}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-smooth-on-top}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e867efc70ec12abb76c0b599c2257902d1595f338e3b2959fe3c74d9f272da7e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c727ccb068d39743b40b4b9fbdbf337255ead7be08304d5b116f90012f06cd7", "source_text": "Suppose <MATH_0001> is a predeformation category admitting a smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002> from a predeformation category\n<MATH_0003>.  Then by\nLemma <REF_0001>\n<MATH_0004> is essentially surjective, so by\nLemma <REF_0002>\n<MATH_0005> is smooth if and only if the\ncomposition <MATH_0006> is smooth, i.e.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0007> is smooth if and only if\n<MATH_0008> is smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15bc7633e3d23b4c91a5c80ad827411f3935067a3de6f31ea62785467e228616", "unit_id": "tag:06HQ:statement"}
